WEBVTT

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.160
Captain Samonji, is something...?

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.330
Captain?

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.620
They're coming back.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.170
Take care of things.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.470
Yes, sir.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:41.100
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.770
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.990
break up foreordination

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:01.870
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.580
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:15.880
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.720
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.850
I need to get ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:32.150
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.650
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.110
wake up your tough intention

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.070
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:42.330
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:48.960
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.500
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.010
break up foreordination

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:09.450
Rage

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.030
Took you long enough!

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.280
Who told you to come right on time?

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.410
I just couldn't wait for you to get here!

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.500
Nevermind that.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.870
Have a seat.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.080
Yes, thank you.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.130
You're so stiff.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:27.130
I didn't call you here to give you a scolding.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.800
You want something to drink?

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.630
I've got a good line-up of alcohol, if nothing else.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.140
I'm on duty.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.680
I see.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.270
Oh, yeah, I heard you and Izumi are close.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:42.230
We were classmates in university.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:44.440
He's an interesting guy, too.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.610
There aren't many people as straight-laced as him.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:50.440
What was his nickname in school, again?

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.450
The "Iron... Virgin"?

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:58.040
Yes, that's it. It fits him perfectly.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.500
He was always so stiff.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:08.880
Well, Izumi's serious nature does make him trustworthy.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.510
So I've put a lot in his hands.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.180
He and I agree on something surprising.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.180
You heard anything from him?

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.680
No, not especially.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.310
Is that so?

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.690
Then I'll tell you.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.150
We're going to lose this war.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.700
Well, I'm right, aren't I?

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.710
The Ingelmia forces are hitting us so hard.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:43.410
No matter how hard your 8th Unit tries,
there's only so much they can do.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.130
We're holding them off in the other theaters for now,

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.340
but it's only a matter of time.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:57.930
By the way, how many of your men have punched a superior officer?

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:01.520
Nine, including you.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.810
You've got moxie, you know that?

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.480
You guys have promise.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:11.070
Depending on what happens,

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:16.410
it might be necessary to change something, even it means punching an officer.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:26.920
You and I are alike.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.590
I disagree.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.090
Do you?

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:35.590
You stick to your guns like that, just as I do.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.270
Anyway, it's a strange thing.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:45.730
Don't you think?

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:46.980
What do you mean?

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:51.520
The pilot of the new model...

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.110
What was it?

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.530
Private Susumu, perhaps?

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.780
Right, Susumu.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:02.620
Nobody would bother to look into the history of a random private.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.540
So we were totally fooled.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.750
Is there a problem with Private Susumu?

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:07.830
Huh?

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.840
Do you really not know?

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.630
What are you talking about?

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:16.420
Oh, my! This is a surprise.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.140
This is a problem.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:20.850
Should I tell you now?

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.300
I don't know.

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:24.140
Please do.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.430
I thought so.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.480
After hearing that much, of course you'd want to hear the rest.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:32.480
Now then, what to do?

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.150
I'll be on my way.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:41.280
Fine, fine. You're always in such a hurry.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:42.740
I'll tell you.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:48.040
That pilot named Tokimune Susumu...

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:53.460
He's the younger brother of Reika Nanjou.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:56.340
Surprised, aren't you?

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:58.380
So was I, at first.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.550
Is a coincidence like that really possible?

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:03.350
Her younger brother, of all people.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.970
And you're his commanding officer.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.850
What a coincidence.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.100
No, it's more like fate.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.070
You're connected by fate.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.950
Is that all?

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:24.410
No, one more thing.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:31.250
Argevollen was supposed to come to me.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.670
It's fine for now.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.250
You can keep it.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:41.220
Kybernes is happily getting better data than ever with it under your command.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.640
Thanks. I'm counting on you.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.440
By the way,

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.030
have you already done it with the girl outside?

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:04.490
Excuse me.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:17.040
Executive Officer!

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:39.230
We've got new weapons, too, right? Show us!

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:42.440
Why don't you want to show it to us?

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:46.240
Now, now, I understand how you feel,

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.700
but the Argevollen Stablis Prima

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:51.830
is Kybernes Manufacturing's secret prototype!

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:53.410
What's going on?
Come on, you can show us a little.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:53.830
Kybernes is about to give your machine a full overhaul.
Come on, you can show us a little.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:55.420
Stingy!
Kybernes is about to give your machine a full overhaul.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:57.710
Sorry. That's the rule.
Kybernes is about to give your machine a full overhaul.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:58.420
Kybernes is about to give your machine a full overhaul.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:00.170
She got a promotion.

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:01.760
That's why she's so excited?

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:02.920
There you are!

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.300
I've been looking for you.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.310
What is this?

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.320
A data logger.

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:21.110
There it is!

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:23.030
I'd like to get started then.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:24.110
Wait a sec.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:25.700
Explain this to me!

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.160
It's a mental test.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:28.410
Mental?

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.700
Also known as an aptitude test.

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:32.120
It's a bit late for that, but...

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:34.660
She's right there.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.620
What do they do if he doesn't pass?

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:40.210
What do we do, I wonder?

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:43.670
Argevollen connects the pilot and machine

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:47.720
via the U-Link system to improve performance.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.140
In other words, knowing about you

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:52.720
means knowing the future of Argevollen.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:54.480
Got it?

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:56.890
Maybe.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.360
Well, don't think about it too much.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:02.400
Just answer the questions I ask honestly.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.360
Okay, let's get started.

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:05.820
First question:

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:09.160
What's wrong?

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.740
Um...

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:15.950
When you take a bath, what do you wash first?

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.040
Does that have anything to do with piloting Argevollen?

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.250
Just answer.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:24.760
My feet.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:27.880
What? That's ridiculous! Normally it's the face!

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:28.800
No, the head.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:29.470
Well, I—

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:29.970
Shut up!
Well, I—

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:30.430
Shut up!

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:31.470
I don't want to know.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.770
What's the point of asking?

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:37.020
Enough!

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:40.020
It's my business whether I wear briefs or boxers!

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:44.270
You already told me what you'd like a girl to whisper to you before you go to sleep,

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.280
so you can answer this!

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:48.570
Okay, next question...

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:50.360
Um...

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:54.330
What's the best thing about Miss Jamie Hazaford?

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:55.740
Wait, what?!

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:57.330
What's with this question?

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:59.790
Does it really say that?

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:01.920
It does. See?

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:06.420
Let me think...

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:08.720
You don't have to answer that.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.590
Yes, I do.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.430
The best thing, huh?

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:18.560
That she's noisy?

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:19.310
Hey!

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:20.600
What do you mean by that?

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:24.860
Is there really a point in this test?

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.980
What? You're doubting me?

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.490
It's all questions that have nothing to do with Argevollen.

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:29.570
Captain!
It's all questions that have nothing to do with Argevollen.

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:30.780
You're so shallow.
Captain!

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:31.740
You're so shallow.

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:33.820
What's important is your inner subconscious.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:35.330
How's it going?

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:37.410
It's like a married couple's comedy routine.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:41.460
Okay, this is my last question.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:45.340
What is Argevollen to you?

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:48.260
What Arge is to me...

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:52.130
A friend?

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.720
No, maybe a partner?

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:57.350
It's more like, well...

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:02.900
Arge is something I can't do without right now... I think.

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:06.690
If I didn't have it,

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:09.320
I don't think I would be as calm

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:12.780
when I look at the squad or at what's going on around me.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:14.780
You call that calm?

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.160
Can't you tell?

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.620
How?

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:19.910
I can't explain it with words!

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:22.620
There's no real point in watching this anymore.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:27.500
Anyway, I see Argevollen as my destiny!

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:32.510
Captain?

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:37.430
That <i>was</i> a really stupid thing to say, I guess.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:50.260
Okay, is everybody here?

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:54.980
All right, I'd like to begin the celebration party for Private Okui,

00:11:54.980 --> 00:12:00.720
who assumed command at Wishpe and was awarded the Medal of Glory Second Rank!

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.450
Okay, say something, Private Okui.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.240
Give me a break.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.950
I don't do that stuff.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.790
Just do it already.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.660
The chief'll start drinking without us.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:19.290
In our last battle, everyone worked together to—

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:22.260
Cheers!

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:23.050
Hey!
Cheers!

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:37.260
It's been months since we've all had drinks together, hasn't it?

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:38.150
Right, Seeker—

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.340
Huh?

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:40.350
He left.

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:41.150
What?!

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:46.230
Today, I'm going to see your
"Top of the Mountain."

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:47.810
You never learn.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:51.660
Well, I don't care, as long as you pay.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.650
Okay, let's go.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:55.000
Sure.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:09.580
Hey, it's the exec!

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.210
Exec!

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:13.550
Oh, hi there, Exec!

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:15.480
Yamanami, move!

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.090
Give her your seat! Shoo!

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:19.300
Executive Officer, please have a seat.

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:20.340
Pardon me.

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:21.220
Not at all.

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:22.480
It's fine.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.480
He can't drink anyway.

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:29.060
Okay, the exec's here too, so let's have a toast.

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.350
Again?

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:32.060
What, Tokimune?

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:34.440
My toasts aren't good enough for you?

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:35.240
N-No...

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:38.150
I'll say a few words, then.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.110
Let's see...

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:42.120
Everyone worked hard this time.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.530
When I heard Okui-kun would be in command,

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:46.340
to be honest, I was worried.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.460
What's with you guys?

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:52.130
But you did well to the end.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:53.460
Good work.

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:54.710
Exec...

00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:58.630
To Independent Unit 8.

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.720
Cheers!

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:10.140
All right, let's drink!

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.700
Everyone sure is having fun, though.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.980
They're just drunk.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:19.040
Look, the chief's passed out.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.700
By the way, what are you looking at?

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:21.950
You're grinning.

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:23.200
Oh, nothing.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:24.990
Your boyfriend?

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:26.370
No, no.

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:30.430
You two shouldn't be like this. Let's have some fun!

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.290
Lorenz-san...

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:33.000
<i>Yay</i>!

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:36.090
Hell yeah! Drunk chicks are sexy!

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:38.670
Hey.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:40.260
Yes?

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:44.430
Why am I the only girl you never go after?

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.640
Huh? Are you?

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:49.060
Why?

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:52.020
Um... I'm gonna get some more to drink.

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:53.140
Wait!

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:55.100
That damn Lorenz.

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:57.770
When he comes back, I'm getting the reason out of him.

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:00.440
Even if he did ask you, you'd turn him down.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:04.250
What's with you, Jamie?
You keep messing with your phone.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.570
Hey, don't...

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:06.960
Hm? Money?

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:08.370
Um, this is...

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:11.000
You got a little promotion and you're already

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:12.470
staring at your bank account?

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:14.710
How much did you get?

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:15.250
Show me!

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:16.000
No!
Show me!

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:16.470
No!

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.210
Show me!

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:18.380
No... Don't...
Show me!

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:19.800
Show me, okay?
No... Don't...

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:20.710
Show me, okay?

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.300
Not there! You'll pull my bra off!

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:27.800
Just give up! So what if it comes off?

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:30.310
You're heavy!

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:36.810
Captain!

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:47.410
At ease.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.000
May I join you?

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.510
Of course!

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:54.080
Captain, sit here.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:54.830
Pardon.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:55.470
Not at all!

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:56.330
That's rare, for the captain to come to a place like this.

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.290
Captain, what will you have?

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.630
Whatever you've got.

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:00.170
Got it.

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:00.500
You're right.
Got it.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:01.260
You're right.

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:03.470
No, no.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:08.110
Your watered-down alcohol isn't good enough for the captain.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.800
You can drink,

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:12.020
but the food here is pretty good, too.

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:13.470
Try this.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:15.310
Hey, you've already eaten some of it!

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:17.660
Hey, come take our order!

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:21.400
Okay, the captain's here!

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:22.500
A toast!

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.540
Cheers!

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:25.020
Captain!

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:28.170
At ease.

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.010
Right... Thank you.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:34.180
You're still stiff. Just relax.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:35.770
O-Okay.

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:40.530
I saw some records on you today.

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:44.520
O-Oh... Is that so?

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:49.570
Are you Reika Nanjou's little brother?

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.950
Y-Yes.

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:58.550
Did you, um...

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:01.330
know my sister?

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:03.790
Yes.

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:10.470
When she died, I was there.

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:18.180
Your sister was forced to participate in an experiment.

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:22.400
An experiment tied up in military secrets.

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:29.030
Your sister died in the midst of it.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:41.680
<i>Exec!</i>

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:57.930
I'm surprised to learn that you were in my sister's squad.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:02.390
How did she meet her end?

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:06.110
It wasn't that simple.

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:10.150
The experiment itself was a failure.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.030
It ended in your sister's death.

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:18.700
Thinking back, it was an idiotic affair.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:20.620
Idiotic?

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:24.330
We knew what would happen from the start.

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:28.720
Her life alone wasn't enough to change anything in that experiment.

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:35.730
She knew it, as well...

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.600
She was a lonely guinea pig

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:43.230
that existed only to be used.

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:51.690
If you knew that, why didn't you stop her?

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:54.070
Why didn't you stop the experiment?

00:19:56.320 --> 00:20:00.790
The captain I know could've done that, right?

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:03.410
I could have.

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:07.080
You're right.

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:11.050
It's possible I could've stopped it.

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.930
But I gave up.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:23.470
Even though I should've known that if it went on, she would die.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:31.690
I'm the one who killed your sister.

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:41.830
What are you doing?!

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:42.620
You idiot!

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:46.620
Say something, damn it!

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:47.750
Hey, let go!

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:48.040
What are you doing?
Hey, let go!

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:48.870
What are you doing?

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:49.290
Stop it! Calm down!

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:51.130
Why? Why?!
Stop it! Calm down!

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:52.750
Why? Why?!

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:05.890
Thanks.

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:06.730
Not at all.

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:11.480
I told them that we'll take care of Private Susumu's punishment.

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:13.230
Good.

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:17.110
What happened today?

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:20.170
What did you discuss with Brigadier General Cowen?

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:29.120
Tokimune Susumu is the younger brother of Reika Nanjou.

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:46.020
The captain told me everything.

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:48.430
That idiot!

00:21:48.430 --> 00:21:50.100
You should know...

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:55.480
about your sister, Reika Nanjou.

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:37.250
Reika Nanjou
Reika Nanjou

00:23:37.250 --> 00:23:39.210
"Reika Nanjou."

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:40.020
Reika Nanjou
Reika Nanjou
